.TH CC 1 "March 15, 1972" "UNIX Fourth Edition" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
v4-cc \- C compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cc
.RB [ \-c ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.I file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I cc
is the UNIX C compiler.
It accepts three types of arguments:
.PP
Arguments whose names end in \fB.c\fR are assumed to be C source programs.
They are compiled, and the object program is written to a file whose name is
that of the source with \fB.o\fR substituted for \fB.c\fR.
.PP
Other arguments, except for \fB\-c\fR, are assumed to be either loader flag
arguments, C-compatible object programs typically produced by an earlier
.I cc
run, or libraries of C-compatible routines.
These programs, together with the results of any compilations specified, are
loaded in the order given to produce an executable program named \fBa.out\fR.
.PP
The \fB\-c\fR argument suppresses the loading phase, as does any syntax error
in any of the routines being compiled.
.PP
If the \fB\-p\fR flag is used, only the macro prepass is run on all files whose
names end in \fB.c\fR.
The expanded source is written to a file whose name is that of the source with
\fB.i\fR substituted for \fB.c\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B file.c
input file
.TP
.B file.o
object file
.TP
.B a.out
loaded output
.TP
.B /tmp/ctm?
temporary file
.TP
.B /lib/c[01]
compiler
.TP
.B /lib/crt0.o
runtime startoff
.TP
.B /lib/libc.a
built-in functions and related routines
.TP
.B /lib/liba.a
system library
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBv4-ld\fR(1)
.SH BUGS
